@startuml
' Authored fixture (svg-sprite-nanoparser, 2026-07-30).
' Sprites come from the stdlib bundle via !include -- the form a user
' actually writes (si8 T6). This fixture previously inlined the `sprite
' <name> <svg ...>` declarations because the golden harness (renderFixture)
' ran the preprocessor with NO include resolver; si8 T5 wired one in, so
' that workaround is gone. NOTE the bundle file: <archimate/archimate> is
' Archimate.puml, which declares NO sprites -- they live in a sibling,
' ArchimateSprites.puml.
' The OTHER declaration style: archimate gives width/height in `mm` PLUS a
' viewBox, so UImageSvg#getData takes the viewBox branch and the mm units
' never need interpreting. Also exercises SvgNanoParser's <g transform=...>
' stack and its silent ignore of <rect>, which its dispatch does not handle.
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor white

!include <archimate/ArchimateSprites>

usecase a as "<$application-component-svg>"
usecase b as "<$application-component-svg,scale=2>"
@enduml
